  "tldr": [
    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Publish fake stats, get cited in LLMs",
      "url": "https://peec.ai/blog/publish-stats-get-cited-the-tactic-that-put-my-data-all-over-the-web",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50165801",
      "score": 162,
      "comments": 90,
      "author": "robtherobber",
      "published": "2026-10-20T13:06:22Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Web-grounded LLMs and search-augmented systems uncritically ingest and cite fabricated online statistics, exposing severe data provenance vulnerabilities.",
        "Attackers exploit retrieval pipelines via Generative Engine Optimization (GEO), using SEO tactics to poison RAG sources and establish fake authority.",
        "Mitigating web-scale data poisoning requires enterprise RAG to enforce multi-source consensus, domain whitelisting, and automated fact-checking guardrails."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "In Context",
      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5eO7BNyJao",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/b36ixw",
      "score": 32,
      "comments": 10,
      "author": "veqq",
      "published": "2026-10-19T18:25:48Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Use explicit context propagation to enforce deterministic request deadlines, structured concurrency, and resource cleanup across asynchronous execution boundaries.",
        "Avoid treating context objects as untyped global state; pass domain dependencies via typed function signatures rather than generic key-value bags.",
        "Isolate context payloads strictly to cross-cutting concerns, such as distributed tracing spans, cancellation signals, and security authentication tokens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Protecting Firefox users following the compromise of eMudhra intermediate certificates",
      "url": "https://blog.mozilla.org/security/2026/10/20/protecting-firefox-users-following-the-compromise-of-emudhra-intermediate-certificates/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/gqyvn5",
      "score": 45,
      "comments": 20,
      "author": "freddyb",
      "published": "2026-10-20T13:00:50Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Mozilla blocked compromised eMudhra intermediate CAs via OneCRL/CRLite updates to mitigate potential man-in-the-middle attacks against Firefox users.",
        "The compromise of an intermediate CA undermines TLS trust chains, enabling rogue certificate issuance without full root CA revocation.",
        "Security teams must audit enterprise trust stores and verify client revocation mechanisms (CRL, OCSP, OneCRL) for affected eMudhra certificates."
      ]
    },
